/-!
# The explicit AS twist field `K(y_j / y_0)` in Galois coordinates

Part of the subproject `Submission/Work/MotAS` (`Work.MotAS`), `MOTIVIC_KDATA_LEAD.md` §6.2:
the Artin–Schreier twist field of the Klein curve is the field generated by the *projectively
normalised* Galois coordinates `y = asM (asRoot g)⁻¹ · κ`, i.e. `K(y_j/y_0)`.

Unlike `Work.MotV5.asTwCoord` (the interpolation model, which contains `asRoot g` and is wrong in
characteristic `5`), `asTwY` uses the **inverse** of the Vandermonde matrix `asM (asRoot g)`, so it
is projectively `σ'`-invariant.  `twistFieldAS_eq` (node **AS-EQ**) identifies this field with
MotV5's `asTwistFieldTrue` (the fixed field of the twisted action `σ' = σ ∘ σS` inside `L(E)`), so
the proved regularity / constants-only / rigidity results of `Work.MotV5` transfer.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace Work.MotAS

open Work.MotV

/-- **The AS twisted coordinates** `y = asM (asRoot g)⁻¹ · κ` in `L(E)`; the twist field is
generated by the ratios `y_j / y_0`. -/
noncomputable def asTwY {𝕜 : Type} [Field 𝕜] (D : Work.MotV.KleinData 𝕜) (g : RatFunc 𝕜)
    (j : Fin 5) : Work.MotV.Om D :=
  ∑ i, algebraMap (Work.MotV.Kb 𝕜) (Work.MotV.Om D)
      ((asM (Work.MotV5.asRoot g))⁻¹ j i) * Work.MotV.kleinCoord D (Work.MotV.Kb 𝕜) i

/-- **The AS twist field** `K(C^AS_g) = K(y_j / y_0)`, `K = 𝕜(t)`: the function field of the
Artin–Schreier twist of the Klein curve by the class of `g`. -/
noncomputable def twistFieldAS {𝕜 : Type} [Field 𝕜] (D : Work.MotV.KleinData 𝕜) (g : RatFunc 𝕜) :
    IntermediateField (RatFunc 𝕜) (Work.MotV.Om D) :=
  IntermediateField.adjoin (RatFunc 𝕜) (Set.range fun j => asTwY D g j / asTwY D g 0)

/-! ## Node AS-EQ

`twistFieldAS_eq` — the identification of `twistFieldAS D g` with MotV5's `asTwistFieldTrue D g τ σS`
— is an open node and lives in `Submission/Work/MotAS/twistFieldAS_eq.lean`.

**Route.**  `⊆`: the ratios `y_j/y_0 = (asM(asRoot g)⁻¹κ)_j / (asM(asRoot g)⁻¹κ)_0` are fixed by
`σ'`: `σ'(κ_i) = λ σS κ_i` (`ASTwistData.hσS`) and `asM (asRoot g + 1) = S · asM (asRoot g)`, so
`σ'` acts by the shift on the `y`'s, hence trivially on their ratios; and `y_j ∈ L(E) = asFieldL D g`
because `asM` has entries in `Kb 𝕜` and `κ_i ∈ L(E)`.  `⊇`: `L · twistFieldAS = Om D` because
`κ = asM(asRoot g) · y` and the `asM`-matrix is invertible, so
`[L(E) : twistFieldAS] ≤ 5 = [L(E) : asTwistFieldTrue]`. -/

end Work.MotAS
